        },
        {
          "id": "line-148",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### ServiceAccount token Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-106",
          "start_line": 148,
          "end_line": 148
        },
        {
          "id": "line-156",
          "kind": "list",
          "text": "- Request a mounted token in a projected volume in your Pod manifest. Kubernetes creates the token and mounts it in the Pod. The token is automatically invalidated when the Pod that it's mounted in is deleted. For details, see Launch a Pod using service account token projection.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-148",
          "start_line": 156,
          "end_line": 156
        },
        {
          "id": "line-429",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Working with Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-1",
          "start_line": 429,
          "end_line": 429
        },
        {
          "id": "line-503",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Using Secrets as files from a Pod\n",
          "parent_id": "line-429",
          "start_line": 503,
          "end_line": 503
        },
        {
          "id": "line-509",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "When a volume contains data from a Secret, and that Secret is updated, Kubernetes tracks this and updates the data in the volume, using an eventually-consistent approach.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-503",
          "start_line": 509,
          "end_line": 509
        },
        {
          "id": "line-511",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "#### Note:\n",
          "parent_id": "line-503",
          "start_line": 511,
          "end_line": 511
        },
        {
          "id": "line-513",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "A container using a Secret as a\nsubPath volume mount does not receive\nautomated Secret updates.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-511",
          "start_line": 513,
          "end_line": 515
        }
      ],
